    "sentence_translations": [
      "Mind the slippery floor",
      "",
      "Paul had been studying Chinese in China for several months.",
      "One day, when he was wandering in a shopping mall, he suddenly needed to use the bathroom.",
      "When he arrived at the bathroom, he noticed that the cleaner had just finished cleaning, leaving the floor wet.",
      "By the side stood a sign saying “slide carefully”.",
      "What a thoughtful shopping mall that reminds people to be careful when sliding, Paul thought to himself.",
      "He then slid into the bathroom, very slowly and very carefully, like he was riding a skateboard.",
      "But Paul then realized that a few people were staring at him oddly.",
      "After he returned to the school, he told his Chinese friend what had happened.",
      "After hearing this, his friend burst into laughter: “Ahh, the board instructs people to mind the slippery floor.”",
      "“It is not telling them to slide into the bathroom.”"
    ]
  }
